          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"schema_version\":\"ai-evaluator-v2/1.1\",\"case_id\":\"5-3\",\"candidate_id\":\"candidate_2\",\"action_assessment\":{\"status\":\"preserved\",\"summary\":\"The main business activities are represented with acceptable paraphrase/grouping, including submission, registration, supervisor decision, change return, rejection, purchasing steps, purchase order generation, waiting, and user notification.\"},\"flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"Core early-to-late ordering is mostly correct, but the required recurrence/continuation after an invalid vendor is not preserved: 'choose a different vendor' does not lead back to vendor selection and subsequent completion steps.\"},\"control_flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"The supervisor’s three-way decision is modeled, but the invalid-vendor branch is wrong: instead of retrying vendor selection until a valid vendor is confirmed, it terminates the process, also bypassing the required downstream notification/completion path.\"},\"main_error_type\":\"wrong_loop_or_recurrence\",\"explanation\":\"The source requires that after approval, if the selected vendor is not valid, the purchase department chooses a different vendor and continues the vendor-selection process until a valid vendor is selected and confirmed, after which the purchase order is sent, delivery/invoice is awaited, and the user is notified. In the generated graph, the 'vendor_invalid' branch goes from 'choose a different vendor' directly to the final node. This wrongly terminates an approved request, omits the required retry/recurrence in vendor selection, and skips later required completion behavior on that path. Aside from this branch, the rest of the process is largely preserved.\",\"overall_score\":0.76,\"severity\":\"moderate\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"ambiguity_flag\":false,\"ambiguity_explanation\":\"\",\"requires_human_review\":false,\"review_reason\":\"\"}"
        }
